---
import ListLayout from '../../layouts/ListLayout.astro';
---

<ListLayout
  title="Accessibility Statement"
  description="Accessibility statement for the Strategic Engineering Laboratory website."
  heading="Accessibility statement"
  intro="This accessibility statement applies to the Strategic Engineering Laboratory research hub."
>
  <div class="statement">
    <p>
      This website is run by the Strategic Engineering Laboratory at the Dyson School of Design
      Engineering, Imperial College London. We want as many people as possible to be able to use
      this website. For example, that means you should be able to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>change colours, contrast levels and fonts using browser or device settings</li>
      <li>zoom in up to 400% without the text spilling off the screen</li>
      <li>navigate most of the website using a keyboard or speech-recognition software</li>
      <li>
        listen to most of the website using a screen reader (including recent versions of JAWS,
        NVDA and VoiceOver)
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We have also made the website text as simple as possible to understand.
      <a href="https://mcmw.abilitynet.org.uk/">AbilityNet</a> has advice on making your device
      easier to use if you have a disability.
    </p>

    <h2>How accessible this website is</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to meet the WCAG 2.2 AA standard throughout. We know some parts of this website are
      not yet fully accessible:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>some images are placeholders and do not yet have a meaningful text alternative</li>
      <li>
        some documents linked from this site (for example, older PDFs) may not be fully
        accessible to screen-reader software
      </li>
      <li>
        some content links out to third-party sites (such as staff profile pages) whose
        accessibility we do not control
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Feedback and contact information</h2>
    <p>
      If you find any problems not listed on this page, think we are not meeting accessibility
      requirements, or need information on this website in a different format such as accessible
      PDF, large print, easy read, audio recording or braille, please contact us:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>email <a href="mailto:design.engineering@imperial.ac.uk">design.engineering@imperial.ac.uk</a></li>
      <li>call +44 (0)20 7589 5111</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We will consider your request and get back to you within 10 working days.</p>

    <h2>Enforcement procedure</h2>
    <p>
      The Equality and Human Rights Commission (EHRC) is responsible for enforcing the Public
      Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) (No. 2) Accessibility Regulations 2018
      (the "accessibility regulations"). If you are not happy with how we respond to your
      complaint, <a href="https://www.equalityadvisoryservice.com/">contact the Equality Advisory
      and Support Service (EASS)</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Technical information about this website's accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Imperial College London is committed to making its website accessible, in accordance with
      the Public Sector Bodies (Websites and Mobile Applications) (No. 2) Accessibility
      Regulations 2018.
    </p>

    <h3>Compliance status</h3>
    <p>
      This website is partially compliant with the
      <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/">Web Content Accessibility Guidelines version 2.2</a>
      AA standard, due to the non-compliances listed below.
    </p>

    <h2>Non-accessible content</h2>
    <p>The content listed below is non-accessible for the following reasons.</p>
    <h3>Non-compliance with the accessibility regulations</h3>
    <p>
      Some images are decorative or placeholder graphics and do not yet carry a text alternative
      that conveys equivalent information. This can fail WCAG 2.2 success criterion 1.1.1
      (non-text content). We plan to add appropriate text alternatives as final imagery is
      published, and new content will meet accessibility standards when added.
    </p>
    <h3>Content that is not within the scope of the accessibility regulations</h3>
    <p>
      Some PDFs and other documents published before 23 September 2018 may not be fully
      accessible. Any new PDFs or documents we publish will meet accessibility standards.
      Third-party content, such as external staff-profile and partner websites, is outside the
      scope of this statement.
    </p>

    <h2>Preparation of this accessibility statement</h2>
    <p>
      This statement was prepared on 17 July 2026. It was last reviewed on 17 July 2026. This
      website was last tested on 17 July 2026 against the WCAG 2.2 AA standard. Testing was
      carried out by the Strategic Engineering Laboratory website team using a combination of
      automated tools and manual keyboard and screen-reader checks.
    </p>
  </div>
</ListLayout>

<style>
  .statement {
    max-width: 70ch;
  }

  .statement h2 {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    margin-top: 44px;
  }

  .statement h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-top: 28px;
  }

  .statement p {
    margin-top: 14px;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .statement ul {
    color: var(--text);
    margin-top: 14px;
    padding-left: 22px;
    line-height: 1.9;
  }

  .statement a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
